TITLE: Model 59 with binary w - equivalent multiple-group regressions;
DATA: FILE = data/salary.dat;
VARIABLE: NAMES=x m y w; USEVARIABLES=x m y;
 GROUPING=w (0=female 1=male);
ANALYSIS: ESTIMATOR=ML; BOOTSTRAP=5000;
MODEL:
 m ON x; y ON m x;
MODEL female:
 m ON x (af); y ON m (bf); y ON x (cf);
 [m] (imf); [y] (iyf);
 m (vm); y (vy);
MODEL male:
 m ON x (am); y ON m (bm); y ON x (cm);
 [m] (imm); [y] (iym);
 m (vm); y (vy);
MODEL CONSTRAINT:
 NEW(ind0 ind1 diff);
 ind0=af*bf; ind1=am*bm; diff=ind1-ind0;
OUTPUT: SAMPSTAT CINTERVAL(BOOTSTRAP);
! Equal residual variances across groups reproduce pooled OLS slopes.
! Slopes/intercepts are free across groups: equivalent to all w interactions.
! Group bootstrap draws preserve group sample sizes in Mplus.
